1
00:00:00,929 --> 00:00:06,262
Welcome to the grand
reopening of Bake Haus of U!

2
00:00:08,110 --> 00:00:10,817
But of course, before we get started,

3
00:00:10,842 --> 00:00:16,821
I want to introduce you to
the family behind this business.

4
00:00:16,893 --> 00:00:22,753
So, let’s begin with
Chard and Iskineport!

5
00:00:24,103 --> 00:00:25,476
- Yes!
- Whoo!

6
00:00:26,093 --> 00:00:27,473
Iskineport!

7
00:00:29,783 --> 00:00:34,920
And of course, there’s also Lola Maxi!

8
00:00:36,640 --> 00:00:40,174
Go Lola, Go Lola, Go Lola! Hey, Hey, Hey!

9
00:00:40,199 --> 00:00:43,910
Go Lola, Go Lola, Go Lola!

10
00:00:44,162 --> 00:00:51,800
Alright, and of course, we also have
the Pers kids – Andres and Tash!

11
00:00:53,928 --> 00:00:55,501
Yay!

12
00:00:59,557 --> 00:01:06,005
Last, but not the least –
Kuya Aga and Ate Cha Pers!

13
00:01:12,466 --> 00:01:14,812
Thank you, thank you, thank
you, thank you, thank you!

14
00:01:14,837 --> 00:01:15,333
Hello!

15
00:01:15,364 --> 00:01:18,734
Thank you so, so, so
much to everyone for

16
00:01:18,758 --> 00:01:22,890
coming to the grand
reopening of Bake Haus of U!

17
00:01:25,290 --> 00:01:28,724
And of course, we’re
all excited to share

18
00:01:28,749 --> 00:01:32,786
with you the upgraded
version of our bakery.

19
00:01:35,654 --> 00:01:36,528
My love!

20
00:01:36,553 --> 00:01:37,233
- Yeah?
- Your turn!

21
00:01:37,258 --> 00:01:40,361
Oh, my turn?!
Ah, we have…um…

22
00:01:40,861 --> 00:01:41,474
Go, Dad!

23
00:01:41,499 --> 00:01:42,871
We have a special guest.

24
00:01:42,896 --> 00:01:50,896
I invited a very close friend of mine who
happens to be a professional pastry chef.

25
00:01:53,011 --> 00:01:56,458
- Wow!
- So, let’s not keep you waiting!

26
00:01:57,098 --> 00:02:00,265
I’m so grateful she agreed to join us.

27
00:02:00,290 --> 00:02:01,290
- Yes!
- Yes!

28
00:02:01,759 --> 00:02:06,239
My friend, Margarita Asistio!

29
00:02:10,641 --> 00:02:14,901
There she is! Hello, hello!

30
00:02:14,948 --> 00:02:16,722
Guys, thank you so much!

31
00:02:16,747 --> 00:02:17,490
Of course!

32
00:02:17,515 --> 00:02:19,105
How could I say no?
You’re such a good friend!

33
00:02:19,129 --> 00:02:22,549
A good, good, good, good,
good, good, good friend!

34
00:02:22,574 --> 00:02:24,062
Oh, yeah!

35
00:02:24,548 --> 00:02:27,481
Cha is so lucky to have you, you know?

36
00:02:28,500 --> 00:02:30,460
And of course, your family!

37
00:02:30,485 --> 00:02:31,428
Oh, thank you, thank you, thank you!

38
00:02:31,453 --> 00:02:35,717
Thank you so much for
inviting me, thank you!

39
00:02:40,137 --> 00:02:43,807
Margarita, please, do the honors!

40
00:02:43,832 --> 00:02:45,094
Oh, of course!

41
00:02:45,119 --> 00:02:48,766
Oh, the mic, the mic, the
mic! Here you go, here you go!

42
00:02:48,791 --> 00:02:51,812
Alright! Let’s count down together!

43
00:02:52,665 --> 00:02:53,905
All together, now!

44
00:02:54,030 --> 00:02:57,950
3…2…1!

45
00:03:02,162 --> 00:03:04,028
Thank you, thank you, thank you, thank you!

46
00:03:04,053 --> 00:03:06,941
Alright! Time to chow!

47
00:03:11,719 --> 00:03:12,712
Let’s dig in!

48
00:03:12,737 --> 00:03:13,737
Hey!

49
00:04:18,405 --> 00:04:21,451
It’s so nice to finally
meet you, Aunt Marga –.

50
00:04:21,476 --> 00:04:21,811
Yeah!

51
00:04:21,836 --> 00:04:23,933
–but how did you and Dad meet?

52
00:04:24,020 --> 00:04:24,823
Ah!

53
00:04:24,848 --> 00:04:28,711
Oh, you know, we were
friends back in college.

54
00:04:28,736 --> 00:04:30,458
We were part of the same group.

55
00:04:32,037 --> 00:04:34,730
- Just friends?
- Yes, friends.

56
00:04:35,365 --> 00:04:38,531
Look at you keeping secrets!

57
00:04:38,877 --> 00:04:40,730
We were friends – before.

58
00:04:40,755 --> 00:04:40,984
Yeah.

59
00:04:41,009 --> 00:04:44,141
But he was persistent
because he courted me!

60
00:04:44,166 --> 00:04:45,925
- What?!
- Whoa!

61
00:04:46,975 --> 00:04:49,135
- Dad?! Really?!
- Huh? For real?!

62
00:04:49,754 --> 00:04:52,387
No, no, no! She turned me down!

63
00:04:52,412 --> 00:04:53,412
Oh.

64
00:04:54,368 --> 00:04:55,942
That makes sense.

65
00:04:55,967 --> 00:04:59,671
- See? She rejected me!
- But then, he courted me again.

66
00:04:59,696 --> 00:05:00,682
- What?!
- Again?!

67
00:05:00,707 --> 00:05:02,108
Yes, and I said yes!

68
00:05:02,133 --> 00:05:03,475
- You what?!
- What?!

69
00:05:04,596 --> 00:05:05,969
Really?!

70
00:05:06,219 --> 00:05:06,686
But…

71
00:05:06,759 --> 00:05:07,759
Dad!

72
00:05:08,178 --> 00:05:09,485
You’re persistent, Dad!

73
00:05:09,537 --> 00:05:13,203
Oh, we became a couple.
But…but…it didn’t last long, right?

74
00:05:13,261 --> 00:05:14,261
Hmm?

75
00:05:14,715 --> 00:05:20,904
But you know, Aga, I wonder
sometimes, what if we continued?

76
00:05:21,585 --> 00:05:22,105
Hmm?

77
00:05:22,130 --> 00:05:24,449
- Huh?
- What if we continued…

78
00:05:24,474 --> 00:05:25,474
- Ah—what?
- Huh?

79
00:05:28,094 --> 00:05:29,094
Well…

80
00:05:30,268 --> 00:05:33,588
- But! It’s just a what-if!
- Exactly!

81
00:05:33,613 --> 00:05:34,190
Ahhh…that’s it.

82
00:05:34,215 --> 00:05:36,807
I’m married now, to
a great veterinarian!

83
00:05:36,832 --> 00:05:38,722
So talented!

84
00:05:38,747 --> 00:05:41,825
What if, Marga…oh, let’s just eat.

85
00:05:41,850 --> 00:05:44,832
Come on, have some
food. Let’s eat! Stay there!

86
00:05:44,857 --> 00:05:46,214
Alright, let’s go, my love. Let’s go.

87
00:05:46,238 --> 00:05:48,859
Alright, let’s eat…wait.

88
00:05:48,884 --> 00:05:51,262
Unbelievable! Look at that, Anne!

89
00:05:52,002 --> 00:05:55,637
They made a few changes and
now they’re having a grand reopening!

90
00:05:57,396 --> 00:06:00,556
Haters gonna hate! That’s
just your Tso K for you!

91
00:06:01,104 --> 00:06:02,724
Tso K-J!

92
00:06:02,945 --> 00:06:06,132
I’m just annoyed because
this guy is so lucky!

93
00:06:06,157 --> 00:06:13,074
Imagine – good-looking, great
kids, an amazing and kind wife!

94
00:06:13,414 --> 00:06:14,494
He has everything!

95
00:06:15,293 --> 00:06:16,293
You’re doing great too!

96
00:06:16,653 --> 00:06:17,653
Oh?

97
00:06:18,030 --> 00:06:19,503
The business is good!

98
00:06:19,528 --> 00:06:21,607
Just the business? That’s it?

99
00:06:21,825 --> 00:06:22,825
BFF!

100
00:06:24,480 --> 00:06:25,480
Again!

101
00:06:25,620 --> 00:06:26,000
Hmm?

102
00:06:26,421 --> 00:06:28,547
You seem fired up again!

103
00:06:28,572 --> 00:06:31,382
Don’t let your blood pressure rise!

104
00:06:31,407 --> 00:06:34,124
You know, if I were
you, I’d just join us here

105
00:06:34,148 --> 00:06:37,351
because none of this
would’ve happened without you.

106
00:06:37,376 --> 00:06:38,651
- That’s right!
- That’s right!

107
00:06:41,718 --> 00:06:45,685
We owe all of this to
everything you’ve lent us.

108
00:06:45,964 --> 00:06:47,511
Thank you so much.

109
00:06:47,807 --> 00:06:53,060
Yes! Yes! Kiss! Speech! Speech!

110
00:06:53,893 --> 00:06:55,753
On one hand, this guy is so shameless.

111
00:06:57,347 --> 00:07:04,026
But on the other hand, maybe I can
expose him to everyone for all the…

112
00:07:04,125 --> 00:07:05,965
terrible things he’s done in my life!

113
00:07:06,330 --> 00:07:07,496
I could, I could!

114
00:07:09,144 --> 00:07:10,144
- BFF…
- That’s possible!

115
00:07:10,628 --> 00:07:11,768
- BFF!
- Yeah?

116
00:07:11,800 --> 00:07:13,494
You’re talking to yourself again.

117
00:07:13,526 --> 00:07:14,987
I just thought of a joke.

118
00:07:16,964 --> 00:07:18,784
Alright, I’ll handle it.

119
00:07:18,828 --> 00:07:21,853
Speech, speech, speech!

120
00:07:21,980 --> 00:07:23,706
Speech, Tso K!

121
00:07:25,261 --> 00:07:27,014
Wait for what I’ll say to you.

122
00:07:27,039 --> 00:07:28,039
Alright.

123
00:08:03,362 --> 00:08:04,362
What happened?!

124
00:08:08,553 --> 00:08:09,553
Where am I?!

125
00:08:17,477 --> 00:08:20,417
Hey! That’s me!

126
00:08:21,538 --> 00:08:22,538
That’s me!

127
00:08:25,679 --> 00:08:26,712
What happened?!

128
00:08:27,159 --> 00:08:28,345
Am I in the hospital?!

129
00:08:28,733 --> 00:08:33,293
Good morning, my love! Good morning!

130
00:08:34,004 --> 00:08:35,004
Oh no!

131
00:08:35,447 --> 00:08:36,501
I’m not in the hospital!

132
00:08:37,967 --> 00:08:38,967
Where am I?!

133
00:08:40,217 --> 00:08:41,217
Am I in heaven?!

134
00:08:42,770 --> 00:08:43,770
What?!

135
00:08:44,291 --> 00:08:45,358
Am I dead?!

136
00:08:45,586 --> 00:08:47,306
What are you talking about, Karl?!

137
00:08:47,697 --> 00:08:48,717
Dead?!

138
00:08:50,096 --> 00:08:53,335
But I – I’m madly in love with you!

139
00:08:53,740 --> 00:08:55,200
Oh, come on, Cha!

140
00:08:55,225 --> 00:08:57,740
Cha, wait a
minute…hold on, hold on!

141
00:08:57,816 --> 00:09:03,258
What we’re doing is
wrong. This isn’t right!

142
00:09:03,309 --> 00:09:05,517
- What?!
- We’re cheating on Aga!

143
00:09:05,542 --> 00:09:06,772
- What?!
- Yes!

144
00:09:06,797 --> 00:09:09,575
Karl, you’re my husband!

145
00:09:11,455 --> 00:09:12,935
What the heck are you talking about?!

146
00:09:22,482 --> 00:09:22,829
Here’s more.

147
00:09:22,854 --> 00:09:23,854
Can I have a slice?

148
00:09:24,140 --> 00:09:24,647
There.

149
00:09:24,672 --> 00:09:25,364
Can I have a slice?

150
00:09:25,389 --> 00:09:27,523
Yeah! You got it. Okay…

151
00:09:28,114 --> 00:09:30,181
- Can you get the…?
- What?

152
00:09:30,542 --> 00:09:30,969
Oh!

153
00:09:31,435 --> 00:09:32,822
Oh! Hi, Dad!

154
00:09:32,875 --> 00:09:33,395
Dad!

155
00:09:33,420 --> 00:09:35,577
- Good morning!
- Good morning, Dad!

156
00:09:35,602 --> 00:09:37,900
- Good morning, good morning!
- Good morning, Dad!

157
00:09:38,267 --> 00:09:39,273
How was your sleep?

158
00:09:41,997 --> 00:09:43,050
I’m your Dad?

159
00:09:43,623 --> 00:09:44,356
- Yeah!
- Yeah!

160
00:09:44,381 --> 00:09:51,401
Of course! Unless you’re
trying to tell us – we’re adopted?!

161
00:09:51,426 --> 00:09:53,432
- Adopted?! Adop–
- No…no…

162
00:09:53,652 --> 00:09:56,459
–Tash, what are you talking
about?! That’s impossible!

163
00:09:56,996 --> 00:09:58,336
Tash, look! Tash!

164
00:09:58,375 --> 00:10:00,402
Hey! Hey, Tash!

165
00:10:00,459 --> 00:10:02,072
We look exactly alike, right?!

166
00:10:03,470 --> 00:10:05,123
Just look at our noses, yeah!

167
00:10:05,148 --> 00:10:06,060
Oh! That’s true!

168
00:10:06,085 --> 00:10:08,640
But wait, I’m getting even more confused!

169
00:10:08,955 --> 00:10:10,095
Why?!

170
00:10:10,120 --> 00:10:13,902
Oh no, oh no, oh
no! What’s going on?!

171
00:10:14,210 --> 00:10:18,365
I’m the one with amnesia! Karl!

172
00:10:19,382 --> 00:10:21,722
Why? What am I
supposed to remember?

173
00:10:22,235 --> 00:10:26,880
That you’re the head of this
family, and you own this bakery.

174
00:10:28,297 --> 00:10:31,430
Does that mean I own all of this?

175
00:10:31,487 --> 00:10:34,086
- Yes! What else do you think, then?!
- Yeah!

176
00:10:34,113 --> 00:10:36,400
It’s like…we switched lives with Aga, huh?

177
00:10:36,571 --> 00:10:38,304
We switched lives with Aga!

178
00:10:52,031 --> 00:10:53,361
- Here’s your order.
- Oh!

179
00:10:57,620 --> 00:10:59,306
Where’s your date?

180
00:10:59,572 --> 00:11:02,472
Oh! Sorry, sorry! I didn’t know.

181
00:11:03,045 --> 00:11:04,045
Chef K!

182
00:11:04,678 --> 00:11:07,953
Oh, Chef K—Kuya Karl!

183
00:11:08,495 --> 00:11:11,101
Wow, you’ve got a different vibe today!

184
00:11:11,220 --> 00:11:13,613
You seem so full of energy! What’s up?

185
00:11:13,697 --> 00:11:14,697
I’m happy!

186
00:11:14,830 --> 00:11:17,757
Everything’s perfect
and beautiful, my love!

187
00:11:17,782 --> 00:11:20,552
My love! I love you, my love!

188
00:11:20,577 --> 00:11:21,842
I love you, my love!

189
00:11:21,867 --> 00:11:26,403
What’s this? PDA this early in the morning?

190
00:11:27,203 --> 00:11:28,536
Oh, why?

191
00:11:28,968 --> 00:11:31,521
What’s wrong with public
displays of affection?

192
00:11:31,546 --> 00:11:35,949
PDA = Pathetic, Dirty, Awkward!

193
00:11:35,974 --> 00:11:37,817
Hey! What? What?

194
00:11:37,842 --> 00:11:38,926
Don’t mind him, Kuya Karl!

195
00:11:38,951 --> 00:11:40,350
You like this, you like this?

196
00:11:40,375 --> 00:11:45,466
Just let it go! That’s how Chef Aga is...

197
00:11:45,659 --> 00:11:47,412
he’s always ruining the mood!

198
00:11:49,453 --> 00:11:52,447
But you know, I used to do the same to Aga.

199
00:11:53,568 --> 00:11:55,208
Wow, I had a terrible
attitude back then.

200
00:11:56,269 --> 00:12:01,300
But honestly, he deserves it!

201
00:12:08,876 --> 00:12:10,683
So, Aga, good morning!

202
00:12:11,122 --> 00:12:13,137
- Good morning, good morning!
- What brings you here?

203
00:12:13,161 --> 00:12:16,795
- Good morning, Cha.
- Oh…

204
00:12:18,058 --> 00:12:20,545
Kuya Karl pushed you! He did!

205
00:12:22,061 --> 00:12:23,136
Do you have bad intentions?

206
00:12:23,160 --> 00:12:25,565
No! I’m just here to collect some debts!

207
00:12:25,590 --> 00:12:26,590
Get aw–.

208
00:12:26,805 --> 00:12:27,825
Your debt!

209
00:12:28,971 --> 00:12:30,084
We owe you money?

210
00:12:30,109 --> 00:12:31,772
- We owe—
- Oh, Aga…

211
00:12:31,867 --> 00:12:33,754
- Cha?
- Can we postpone it until tomorrow?

212
00:12:33,779 --> 00:12:34,913
Please, if that’s okay.

213
00:12:35,337 --> 00:12:38,197
Cha, don’t worry about the debt!

214
00:12:38,503 --> 00:12:41,049
Since you said so,
don’t even think about it!

215
00:12:41,202 --> 00:12:43,489
No problem, forget the debt!

216
00:12:43,641 --> 00:12:46,015
But you do owe me a favor!

217
00:12:46,468 --> 00:12:47,494
Wait, wait!

218
00:12:48,098 --> 00:12:50,151
How exactly do we owe you a favor?

219
00:12:50,619 --> 00:12:54,466
Well, if I hadn’t stopped pursuing Cha,

220
00:12:54,967 --> 00:12:58,013
I would be the one
standing there now—with her.

221
00:12:58,053 --> 00:12:59,053
Hey!

222
00:12:59,511 --> 00:13:01,737
I’d be the one in your
place right now—with her!

223
00:13:02,220 --> 00:13:07,703
Well, as they say—haters gonna hate, right?

224
00:13:07,728 --> 00:13:10,527
- True!
- But I get it.

225
00:13:10,552 --> 00:13:18,552
He’s jealous because my love and I
are happy together, and he’s single.

226
00:13:21,075 --> 00:13:21,662
Single!

227
00:13:21,687 --> 00:13:22,288
Is that what happiness looks like?

228
00:13:22,366 --> 00:13:24,359
Where’s the proof?

229
00:13:24,607 --> 00:13:25,967
That’s what you’re bragging about?

230
00:13:26,831 --> 00:13:27,971
Wait a minute…

231
00:13:28,291 --> 00:13:29,311
Honeybunch!

232
00:13:29,937 --> 00:13:32,590
Yes?! Yes! I’m here!

233
00:13:34,497 --> 00:13:37,271
Oh! Is this Karl and Cha?

234
00:13:37,296 --> 00:13:38,512
- Yes!
- Hi!

235
00:13:38,576 --> 00:13:41,936
Nice to meet you! I’ve heard
so many good things about you!

236
00:13:41,961 --> 00:13:44,875
Wow! Wow!

237
00:13:44,900 --> 00:13:46,808
- Nice to meet you!
- Aga, I’m happy for you!

238
00:13:46,833 --> 00:13:47,558
Yes!

239
00:13:47,583 --> 00:13:51,800
At least now your life is
sweet, just like ours! Right?

240
00:13:51,825 --> 00:13:55,225
That’s not sweet at all! This is
what sweet really looks like, see?

241
00:13:56,533 --> 00:13:57,833
Like this, see?

242
00:13:57,858 --> 00:13:59,151
Let’s see!

243
00:14:02,001 --> 00:14:03,001
Hey!

244
00:14:03,400 --> 00:14:05,013
That Aga!

245
00:14:05,302 --> 00:14:08,435
Even though our lives
swapped, he’s still ruining mine!

246
00:14:10,282 --> 00:14:13,929
Kuya K, don’t mind Kuya Aga anymore!

247
00:14:14,175 --> 00:14:18,353
He’s been a thorn in
our side for so long now!

248
00:14:18,825 --> 00:14:20,038
True, Kuya Karl!

249
00:14:20,840 --> 00:14:25,244
And if you think about it,
you’re still luckier than Kuya Aga.

250
00:14:25,406 --> 00:14:26,572
You’re the real winner here.

251
00:14:27,885 --> 00:14:29,352
You’re right. That’s true.

252
00:14:30,417 --> 00:14:31,985
This is the real life...

253
00:14:32,898 --> 00:14:36,969
if I’m dreaming, I don’t want to wake up.

254
00:14:38,295 --> 00:14:41,468
And, honestly, having
assistants feels great, doesn’t it?

255
00:14:42,674 --> 00:14:44,827
Hey, fan me.

256
00:14:44,852 --> 00:14:47,493
You know, I’ve been wanting to
give you orders for a long time.

257
00:14:47,518 --> 00:14:49,246
- Yes, sir!
- I’ll fan you despite my nervousness!

258
00:14:49,270 --> 00:14:50,270
Exactly.

259
00:14:50,722 --> 00:14:53,709
Bake A…Bake A. It’s good.

260
00:14:54,462 --> 00:14:55,069
Looks nice.

261
00:14:55,361 --> 00:14:56,621
- Honeybunch…
- Yes?!

262
00:14:56,646 --> 00:14:57,646
I have a question.

263
00:14:57,839 --> 00:14:58,559
Yes?

264
00:14:58,584 --> 00:15:01,682
If I weren’t a pastry chef,
would you still love me?

265
00:15:02,042 --> 00:15:03,282
Of course!

266
00:15:04,139 --> 00:15:05,139
Of course!

267
00:15:05,385 --> 00:15:07,872
What if I didn’t have a
job, would you still love me?

268
00:15:08,557 --> 00:15:09,991
Of course!

269
00:15:10,944 --> 00:15:12,604
Definitely!

270
00:15:12,629 --> 00:15:15,372
What if…what if…I were a fly,

271
00:15:16,640 --> 00:15:17,833
would you still love me?

272
00:15:18,966 --> 00:15:20,419
How would you even become a fly?

273
00:15:21,227 --> 00:15:22,974
Yes—of course! Even as a fly!

274
00:15:22,999 --> 00:15:23,487
Really?

275
00:15:23,512 --> 00:15:24,664
Yes! I’d still love you!

276
00:15:24,689 --> 00:15:25,360
You’re crazy.

277
00:15:25,530 --> 00:15:26,637
Why?

278
00:15:27,352 --> 00:15:30,639
Because if I were a fly, I’d land
on you, and that’s dirty, right?

279
00:15:30,664 --> 00:15:32,615
What would you do?
You’d probably swat me away!

280
00:15:33,425 --> 00:15:34,365
Yes, I’d swat you away!

281
00:15:34,390 --> 00:15:36,634
See! You’d swat me away!

282
00:15:36,659 --> 00:15:38,620
That means you don’t love me!

283
00:15:38,645 --> 00:15:44,394
No! I mean…I’d swat—oh,
no, wait…I’d…become a fly too.

284
00:15:44,422 --> 00:15:47,111
So we could still be together! Right?

285
00:15:47,136 --> 00:15:49,318
- Really?
- I told you already!

286
00:15:50,324 --> 00:15:53,899
- I love you, Honeybunch!
- And I love you too, very much!

287
00:15:54,319 --> 00:15:57,671
Oh, what’s the big deal? Two
flies in love—that’s fine by me!

288
00:15:59,166 --> 00:16:01,686
- Okay, back to work. Go on.
- Alright!

289
00:16:01,711 --> 00:16:02,630
- I’m leaving!
- Okay!

290
00:16:02,655 --> 00:16:04,640
Okay? I’ll see you later, alright?

291
00:16:04,665 --> 00:16:06,424
- See ya!
- Okay dokey dokes!

292
00:16:06,902 --> 00:16:07,902
Cupcake!

293
00:16:09,643 --> 00:16:11,411
- Oh, this way!
- Oh, right, this way!

294
00:16:13,300 --> 00:16:14,520
You guys!

295
00:16:15,866 --> 00:16:16,866
Alright!

296
00:16:22,712 --> 00:16:24,145
So, Anne? What do you think?

297
00:16:24,745 --> 00:16:27,938
Tito Aga, isn’t Tita
Marga a little weird?

298
00:16:28,497 --> 00:16:32,177
Not really. She’s like
that, but she’s really kind!

299
00:16:32,392 --> 00:16:33,392
Tito Aga!

300
00:16:33,772 --> 00:16:34,658
How are you?

301
00:16:34,735 --> 00:16:37,009
- Oh, hey Andres!
- Oh, we’re just inviting Anne

302
00:16:37,097 --> 00:16:38,730
to hang out, if it’s okay with you.

303
00:16:39,121 --> 00:16:40,601
- You’re inviting her out?
- Yes, sir.

304
00:16:40,741 --> 00:16:41,741
Anne?

305
00:16:42,484 --> 00:16:44,743
Anne, be careful with
guys like this, okay?

306
00:16:45,125 --> 00:16:49,518
They’re smooth
operators—just like his dad!

307
00:16:50,042 --> 00:16:51,475
Don’t fall for it!

308
00:16:51,513 --> 00:16:52,486
Just don’t.

309
00:16:52,511 --> 00:16:53,610
- Don’t go—
- Hey, Aga!

310
00:16:53,635 --> 00:16:55,195
Why are you talking to my son that way?

311
00:16:55,341 --> 00:16:55,787
Huh?

312
00:16:55,987 --> 00:16:58,347
And I heard you raising your
voice. Are you yelling at him?

313
00:16:58,395 --> 00:16:59,959
- No—
- Don’t yell at my kids!

314
00:17:00,883 --> 00:17:03,683
And you—why are you still
here? Don’t you have a curfew?

315
00:17:04,055 --> 00:17:07,095
You’re so strict, Dad.

316
00:17:07,252 --> 00:17:09,712
You know what, Dad? We’re adults.

317
00:17:09,845 --> 00:17:10,852
We’re adults, Dad.

318
00:17:10,877 --> 00:17:12,602
No, you’re not! Go home, now!

319
00:17:14,882 --> 00:17:15,882
Alright, sir.

320
00:17:18,433 --> 00:17:19,973
Stop arguing!

321
00:17:21,046 --> 00:17:22,746
Why are you yelling at your kids?

322
00:17:26,520 --> 00:17:27,520
- Aga…
- What?

323
00:17:27,637 --> 00:17:34,307
Don’t meddle in how I run my life, okay?

324
00:17:35,593 --> 00:17:42,897
I’m in charge here! Understand?

325
00:17:42,924 --> 00:17:46,304
Don’t piss me off, alright?

326
00:17:46,503 --> 00:17:49,018
Ouch, ouch, Karl. Karl, Karl…Karl…Karl?

327
00:17:49,825 --> 00:17:51,758
Not every day is a
happy day for you.

328
00:17:51,783 --> 00:17:52,185
Oh?

329
00:17:52,610 --> 00:17:53,610
Same with me.

330
00:17:54,010 --> 00:17:57,216
Because I heard you’re
having family issues.

331
00:17:58,378 --> 00:17:58,891
What?!

332
00:17:59,335 --> 00:18:01,495
- What family issues?
- Yes!

333
00:18:02,302 --> 00:18:04,049
Where’d you hear that, gossipmonger?

334
00:18:04,074 --> 00:18:06,164
I just heard it, I’m not gossiping!

335
00:18:06,189 --> 00:18:09,441
You’re a gossip! How dare you meddle in
my family—want to settle this with a fight?

336
00:18:09,465 --> 00:18:12,112
- Hey! Stop, stop, stop!
- You’re pushing it!

337
00:18:12,137 --> 00:18:13,807
Hold on! Hold on!

338
00:18:14,299 --> 00:18:16,099
Violence is not allowed here.

339
00:18:16,124 --> 00:18:18,538
If you want, let’s settle
this with a dance showdown!

340
00:18:18,563 --> 00:18:19,563
Music!

341
00:18:20,531 --> 00:18:23,084
What dance showdown?
What are you talking about? Hey!

342
00:18:23,109 --> 00:18:28,392
Music? I don’t want that! I
don’t like those things! Huh?

343
00:18:28,417 --> 00:18:29,450
- Oh!
- Ah!

344
00:18:31,803 --> 00:18:34,423
My daughter taught me this, Tash!

345
00:18:34,448 --> 00:18:35,556
And her moves too!

346
00:18:35,581 --> 00:18:39,643
You’d think, she’s
teaching me these things!

347
00:18:39,827 --> 00:18:40,827
Try it…wow!

348
00:18:49,485 --> 00:18:50,791
Is there really a problem?

349
00:18:52,770 --> 00:18:57,444
I’ve got my dream—Cha.

350
00:19:03,207 --> 00:19:04,214
So what’s the issue?

351
00:19:23,877 --> 00:19:24,877
Hey!

352
00:19:35,991 --> 00:19:41,009
Ugh, it’s just my first time asking.

353
00:19:41,877 --> 00:19:44,591
Do I still feel the same way
about her as I did before?

354
00:19:45,816 --> 00:19:48,416
You know, it’s different
when you’re courting someone

355
00:19:48,755 --> 00:19:51,482
versus when they’re already your spouse.

356
00:19:53,042 --> 00:19:54,042
It’s just… different.

357
00:19:57,571 --> 00:19:58,571
Oh, gosh.

358
00:20:02,503 --> 00:20:04,543
- Good morning!
- What the heck is happening to her?

359
00:20:04,945 --> 00:20:06,465
Good morning, my love!

360
00:20:06,490 --> 00:20:07,490
Morning.

361
00:20:10,816 --> 00:20:11,343
Sorry...

362
00:20:11,480 --> 00:20:12,480
Are you okay?

363
00:20:13,060 --> 00:20:14,820
I couldn’t sleep.

364
00:20:15,816 --> 00:20:18,183
I’m too mad at Aga.

365
00:20:19,540 --> 00:20:22,920
Can you believe he told
me we have family problems?

366
00:20:30,157 --> 00:20:31,157
Do we?

367
00:20:33,658 --> 00:20:34,152
Oh!

368
00:20:34,177 --> 00:20:35,441
Don’t let it bother you, my love!

369
00:20:35,465 --> 00:20:38,290
Wait, so we do?! You’re
not answering! There really is!

370
00:20:38,536 --> 00:20:41,910
Do you want to make a sibling
for Atasha and Andres instead?

371
00:20:41,935 --> 00:20:43,294
Goodness, what is this?!

372
00:20:43,319 --> 00:20:44,991
Come here and hug me, quickly!

373
00:20:45,016 --> 00:20:46,558
Let’s just make a sibling
for Atasha and Andres!

374
00:20:46,582 --> 00:20:50,252
Cha, hold on, hold on!
You’re being way too frisky!

375
00:20:51,632 --> 00:20:52,980
What is it with you?!

376
00:20:53,046 --> 00:20:54,046
What, Karl?

377
00:20:54,192 --> 00:20:55,259
I’m not in the mood!

378
00:20:59,968 --> 00:21:01,128
What’s gotten into him?!

379
00:21:02,127 --> 00:21:03,434
You keep eating.

380
00:21:03,459 --> 00:21:05,149
This is sardines;
it’s nutritious.

381
00:21:07,202 --> 00:21:08,202
Delicious!

382
00:21:09,987 --> 00:21:11,167
You’re like a child.

383
00:21:13,517 --> 00:21:14,751
Sardines again?!

384
00:21:15,412 --> 00:21:17,372
Why is it always sardines?!

385
00:21:17,716 --> 00:21:22,349
My love, it’s because
our grocery budget is tight.

386
00:21:28,118 --> 00:21:30,095
Look at this—it’s so spicy!

387
00:21:31,337 --> 00:21:32,337
Give me some water!

388
00:21:32,560 --> 00:21:35,247
Kuya Karl, we don’t
have water. It got cut off.

389
00:21:36,153 --> 00:21:40,918
Oh, and there’s also
a disconnection notice.

390
00:21:44,011 --> 00:21:45,190
Electricity’s been cut, too?!

391
00:21:45,215 --> 00:21:46,215
Mm-hmm.

392
00:21:47,392 --> 00:21:49,752
Why is this happening?! Are
we really struggling this much?!

393
00:21:51,317 --> 00:21:54,384
Andres, Tash! What if you two get jobs?!

394
00:21:56,098 --> 00:21:57,572
We have jobs, Dad.

395
00:21:57,975 --> 00:22:00,861
But you called us home to help
with the bake shop, didn’t you?!

396
00:22:01,143 --> 00:22:03,430
Wow, Dad, is this still our fault?

397
00:22:04,111 --> 00:22:08,271
You know what, Dad,
you’re the best dad ever!

398
00:22:11,458 --> 00:22:13,011
Atasha! Andres!

399
00:22:13,802 --> 00:22:14,689
Atasha! Andre–.

400
00:22:14,714 --> 00:22:15,714
Oh...

401
00:22:18,696 --> 00:22:20,276
Awkward!

402
00:22:20,942 --> 00:22:23,429
Uh! We’ll go now.

403
00:22:28,163 --> 00:22:34,610
Karl, even in our family,
we have problems too.

404
00:22:35,210 --> 00:22:39,517
Like me, I fight with my dad.

405
00:22:40,249 --> 00:22:43,336
But eventually, my anger disappeared.

406
00:22:44,640 --> 00:22:45,640
How did it go away?

407
00:22:46,854 --> 00:22:49,261
You know Roman, right?

408
00:22:49,576 --> 00:22:54,663
He came into my room and
said we should do something.

409
00:22:54,961 --> 00:22:55,961
Ew!

410
00:22:56,849 --> 00:22:59,189
Ew?! He said we should elope!

411
00:22:59,214 --> 00:23:01,057
That’s what he wanted to do!

412
00:23:01,082 --> 00:23:02,443
I don’t know with you!

413
00:23:02,891 --> 00:23:06,165
Honestly, I’ve always been
on Aga’s side, even before!

414
00:23:06,444 --> 00:23:08,517
Unlike you, I’m getting thinner here!

415
00:23:09,219 --> 00:23:10,219
Unbelievable!

416
00:23:11,600 --> 00:23:13,020
Move over; I don’t fit!

417
00:23:16,830 --> 00:23:17,830
Well, move!

418
00:23:22,846 --> 00:23:23,852
Here, have a snack.

419
00:23:24,032 --> 00:23:26,072
- Thanks.
- Don’t worry about it, it’s on the house.

420
00:23:26,389 --> 00:23:28,076
That Karl is something else!

421
00:23:28,597 --> 00:23:34,530
Sometimes I think maybe he’s not
cut out to be a father or a husband.

422
00:23:37,030 --> 00:23:43,906
It’s okay! Just remember
I’m always here for you.

423
00:23:45,052 --> 00:23:46,252
Thanks, Aga.

424
00:23:46,446 --> 00:23:46,792
Mm-hmm.

425
00:23:47,050 --> 00:23:48,050
Thank you...

426
00:23:48,289 --> 00:23:52,115
you really are my shoulder to cry on
whenever Karl and I have problems.

427
00:23:52,344 --> 00:23:53,957
I get that a lot!

428
00:23:55,552 --> 00:23:56,379
Hank you, really.

429
00:23:56,558 --> 00:23:58,345
You know, sometimes I wonder,

430
00:24:00,835 --> 00:24:06,588
what if I had gone ahead
with my plan to court you?

431
00:24:06,815 --> 00:24:07,122
Hmm?

432
00:24:07,268 --> 00:24:09,208
If I did, and we ended up together,

433
00:24:09,772 --> 00:24:12,612
maybe you wouldn’t have
the problems you have now.

434
00:24:14,267 --> 00:24:15,267
Whoa!

435
00:24:16,150 --> 00:24:17,150
Oh?!

436
00:24:17,965 --> 00:24:19,099
What do you take me for, deaf?!

437
00:24:19,123 --> 00:24:20,123
Of course not!

438
00:24:20,387 --> 00:24:21,740
What did I just hear?!

439
00:24:21,792 --> 00:24:24,159
Uh, I don’t know! What did you hear?!

440
00:24:24,184 --> 00:24:26,426
What?! What?! What?! Is there
something going on between you two?!

441
00:24:26,450 --> 00:24:26,941
No!

442
00:24:26,966 --> 00:24:28,156
- None!
- There is! I heard it!

443
00:24:28,180 --> 00:24:29,580
No, come on!

444
00:24:29,605 --> 00:24:30,888
You traitors!

445
00:24:30,913 --> 00:24:31,913
What?!

446
00:24:32,510 --> 00:24:33,510
Traitor!

447
00:24:33,572 --> 00:24:34,285
Traitor!

448
00:24:34,310 --> 00:24:36,126
- What, Karl?!
- What are you doing with my wife?!

449
00:24:36,150 --> 00:24:36,911
What am I doing?!

450
00:24:36,936 --> 00:24:38,295
Are you courting my woman?!

451
00:24:38,381 --> 00:24:39,355
Huh?! She’s my wife!

452
00:24:39,380 --> 00:24:41,283
I’m not courting—ow! Ow!

453
00:24:41,308 --> 00:24:43,953
- I don’t want to fight!
- Ow, ow, ow!

454
00:24:43,978 --> 00:24:45,437
Stop it! No, go ahead!

455
00:24:45,462 --> 00:24:46,618
No, stop! Stop, stop!

456
00:24:49,009 --> 00:24:50,476
I said stop!

457
00:24:50,501 --> 00:24:51,802
This is wrestling! Wrestling!

458
00:24:52,744 --> 00:24:56,580
See, you’re hurting! You’re hurting!

459
00:24:56,605 --> 00:24:58,218
I don’t care, we’re fighting!

460
00:24:59,475 --> 00:25:01,662
Does it hurt? Does it hurt?!

461
00:25:02,665 --> 00:25:05,058
Oh, see?! You’re completely
defeated now, aren’t you?!

462
00:25:05,337 --> 00:25:08,650
If you hadn’t stopped me, I
would’ve really hit Aga hard.

463
00:25:09,018 --> 00:25:12,698
You know, if I didn’t stop you,
you’d be the one who got hurt!

464
00:25:12,723 --> 00:25:13,880
You were in the line of fire!

465
00:25:13,904 --> 00:25:16,597
No! You’re just protecting Aga!

466
00:25:16,791 --> 00:25:19,038
Ugh, Karl, I don’t know about you anymore!

467
00:25:19,393 --> 00:25:25,007
I’m trying to understand
you, but I just can’t!

468
00:25:25,680 --> 00:25:28,034
And I’m not happy anymore!

469
00:25:28,440 --> 00:25:29,440
Cha, huh?!

470
00:25:30,046 --> 00:25:31,320
Don’t talk to me anymore!

471
00:25:31,345 --> 00:25:32,345
Cha!

472
00:25:33,381 --> 00:25:34,381
Chacha!

473
00:25:37,062 --> 00:25:39,708
Oh, where are you going?

474
00:25:40,194 --> 00:25:41,387
You know, Dad, we’re leaving.

475
00:25:41,775 --> 00:25:43,448
There’s nothing for
us here anymore.

476
00:25:43,730 --> 00:25:45,710
Yeah, we’re going back to Singapore, Dad.

477
00:25:51,602 --> 00:25:52,602
Fine!

478
00:25:52,952 --> 00:25:53,952
Leave!

479
00:25:55,430 --> 00:25:56,430
Leave me!

480
00:25:57,471 --> 00:25:58,891
All of you, just leave!

481
00:25:59,064 --> 00:26:00,064
Go ahead!

482
00:26:00,143 --> 00:26:02,677
Everyone leave… wait, the lights went out?

483
00:26:03,603 --> 00:26:04,603
What’s that?!

484
00:26:05,194 --> 00:26:06,194
A blackout?!

485
00:26:07,377 --> 00:26:08,524
A blackout…

486
00:26:09,112 --> 00:26:10,732
even the lights are gone.

487
00:26:11,678 --> 00:26:13,592
Blackout…

488
00:26:14,484 --> 00:26:16,744
Hey, I’m sorry about earlier.

489
00:26:16,785 --> 00:26:21,952
I’m not usually like that.
I know they’re family people.

490
00:26:22,566 --> 00:26:23,993
We’ve been together a long time.

491
00:26:24,383 --> 00:26:27,516
Sometimes I wonder… Aga…

492
00:26:27,725 --> 00:26:29,385
- Hmm?
- …do you really love me?

493
00:26:29,664 --> 00:26:31,656
I love you so much.

494
00:26:31,809 --> 00:26:35,215
Even if you turned into a fly or
a grasshopper, I’d still love you.

495
00:26:35,911 --> 00:26:37,344
Wow, a grasshopper?!

496
00:26:37,369 --> 00:26:39,635
- Did you hear that, my love?
- I’d even marry you.

497
00:26:39,699 --> 00:26:40,672
- Huh?!
- Wait, marriage?!

498
00:26:40,697 --> 00:26:41,697
Oh my God!

499
00:26:42,404 --> 00:26:45,151
So, where’s this coming from – hello?

500
00:26:45,746 --> 00:26:47,392
- You’re crazy!
- Why?

501
00:26:47,440 --> 00:26:49,534
- Marriage?
- Yes, I’ll marry you!

502
00:26:50,175 --> 00:26:54,257
You know, I saw the way
you looked at Cha earlier.

503
00:26:56,298 --> 00:26:58,131
That’s how you
used to look at me.

504
00:26:58,357 --> 00:26:59,357
Used to.

505
00:26:59,508 --> 00:27:00,762
But not anymore.

506
00:27:02,057 --> 00:27:04,913
So, Aga, if you’re going
to propose marriage,

507
00:27:06,983 --> 00:27:09,063
it should be because you
want to be with that person.

508
00:27:09,854 --> 00:27:11,101
Not because…

509
00:27:11,126 --> 00:27:12,609
Someone proposed to me before?

510
00:27:12,634 --> 00:27:16,228
…you don’t want to be alone.
Remember that, okay?

511
00:27:16,617 --> 00:27:17,617
Got it.

512
00:27:17,832 --> 00:27:19,892
Oh, just give me a hug. Just give me a hug.

513
00:27:19,917 --> 00:27:22,002
- Hey!
- They’re hugging!

514
00:27:22,646 --> 00:27:23,992
It reminds me of my younger days…

515
00:27:24,017 --> 00:27:25,427
- Take care, okay?
- Take care…

516
00:27:25,452 --> 00:27:28,918
- Kiss on the lips! Kiss on the lips!
- Kiss on the lips!

517
00:27:28,943 --> 00:27:30,598
- Nothing? Not even on the cheek?
- Your, uh…

518
00:27:30,622 --> 00:27:31,990
I can’t text you!

519
00:27:32,015 --> 00:27:36,571
- No signal! Gosh! There’s no signal here!
- I can’t hear you, I’m texting!

520
00:27:36,702 --> 00:27:39,382
- Is this it? Bye-bye now?
- Yeah, bye!

521
00:27:40,685 --> 00:27:43,398
I love you! I really, really love you.

522
00:27:43,661 --> 00:27:47,188
Poor Kuya Aga, Ate Marga broke up with him!

523
00:27:47,250 --> 00:27:49,403
- It looks like it’s over!
- It’s okay, Chef Aga.

524
00:27:49,428 --> 00:27:49,830
Huh?

525
00:27:50,431 --> 00:27:52,264
- It’s okay!
- What’s okay?

526
00:27:52,289 --> 00:27:53,554
- It’s okay!
- It’s nothing!

527
00:27:53,579 --> 00:27:56,243
But you know, I remember that woman.

528
00:27:56,529 --> 00:28:00,379
Isn’t she the one whose memory
you buried in your Alabang house?

529
00:28:00,404 --> 00:28:01,856
Psst, psst, here, I’m leaving this for you.

530
00:28:01,880 --> 00:28:04,289
You buried her memory in
the foundation of the house?

531
00:28:04,314 --> 00:28:06,562
Why… what?

532
00:28:09,352 --> 00:28:10,352
Didn’t you?

533
00:28:11,120 --> 00:28:14,199
Why are you carrying
that, what’s it for, Chef?

534
00:28:14,224 --> 00:28:15,422
It’s for you!

535
00:28:15,447 --> 00:28:17,939
- Why?
- I’m leaving now.

536
00:28:17,964 --> 00:28:19,661
- Fine, leave.
- I don’t want to hear about this anymore!

537
00:28:19,685 --> 00:28:21,305
He’s still our idol, though!

538
00:28:21,758 --> 00:28:22,898
Thank you, Chef.

539
00:28:22,955 --> 00:28:27,802
You know, Chef Aga will never run
out of admirers! He has so many women!

540
00:28:28,125 --> 00:28:29,578
Wow! He’s really my idol!

541
00:28:29,603 --> 00:28:31,373
Mmm, guys, grab some, it’s delicious.

542
00:28:31,398 --> 00:28:32,398
Mmm…

543
00:28:32,530 --> 00:28:33,804
- Tso K!
- So what?

544
00:28:34,732 --> 00:28:35,732
That’s your idol?

545
00:28:36,644 --> 00:28:38,951
- Yes! Because…
- Chef Aga is so kind!

546
00:28:38,976 --> 00:28:40,690
What does he have that I don’t?!

547
00:28:40,715 --> 00:28:41,774
He’s kind!

548
00:28:41,854 --> 00:28:44,894
And also, Kuya Karl, you’re cute.

549
00:28:45,167 --> 00:28:45,674
Hmm?

550
00:28:45,699 --> 00:28:49,565
But Chef Aga is handsome!

551
00:28:49,952 --> 00:28:51,539
There’s a big difference.

552
00:28:51,915 --> 00:28:59,915
Chef Aga is super, super, to
the highest level, yes, amazing!

553
00:29:00,931 --> 00:29:06,136
Hey! Stop it! Stop it!
You’re being hurtful!

554
00:29:06,161 --> 00:29:08,795
Sorry, sorry, Kuya
Karl. I got carried away.

555
00:29:09,865 --> 00:29:12,832
But it’s okay. I have an idea.

556
00:29:13,735 --> 00:29:17,872
Aga, get ready.

557
00:29:18,512 --> 00:29:19,586
Get ready!

558
00:29:21,058 --> 00:29:21,705
Tso K…

559
00:29:21,730 --> 00:29:22,730
Move aside!

560
00:29:23,744 --> 00:29:25,197
Let’s put this here.

561
00:29:29,540 --> 00:29:31,553
Oh? BFF!

562
00:29:31,718 --> 00:29:32,328
Hmm?

563
00:29:32,353 --> 00:29:33,353
Are you drunk?

564
00:29:35,221 --> 00:29:36,221
Nope!

565
00:29:37,498 --> 00:29:39,765
Hey! Nope! Nothing, nothing!

566
00:29:40,499 --> 00:29:42,896
- You’re drunk!
- I’m not!

567
00:29:43,059 --> 00:29:43,393
Huh?

568
00:29:43,418 --> 00:29:45,374
Here, see! Still think I’m drunk?

569
00:29:45,980 --> 00:29:47,180
Look at me standing up right!

570
00:29:47,262 --> 00:29:49,348
- So, you’re not drunk?
- No, I’m not drunk.

571
00:29:49,856 --> 00:29:52,983
No… BFF, I just wanted to apologize.

572
00:29:54,107 --> 00:29:54,750
Apologize?

573
00:29:54,775 --> 00:29:55,775
Yeah.

574
00:29:57,082 --> 00:29:58,082
For what?

575
00:29:58,778 --> 00:30:03,410
For what happened with Cha,
I didn’t mean anything bad.

576
00:30:03,945 --> 00:30:06,039
It just so happened we were talking.

577
00:30:06,706 --> 00:30:12,566
From now on, I won’t go near
her, or even see her again.

578
00:30:12,591 --> 00:30:13,950
- Hmm.
- I’m really sorry.

579
00:30:15,152 --> 00:30:16,140
Okay!

580
00:30:16,165 --> 00:30:16,545
Mmm!

581
00:30:16,583 --> 00:30:20,395
Sorry! But I’m also sorry…

582
00:30:21,237 --> 00:30:21,663
Why?

583
00:30:21,688 --> 00:30:22,728
…for what I’m about to do.

584
00:30:23,440 --> 00:30:25,160
What are you going to do?
Why are you sorry?

585
00:30:25,803 --> 00:30:31,807
You know, Aga, when I
became you, I was happy.

586
00:30:33,494 --> 00:30:37,661
But I can’t handle your life’s problems!

587
00:30:38,945 --> 00:30:42,608
So, here’s what I thought of…

588
00:30:43,309 --> 00:30:45,729
What’s that? Wh-what are you doing?

589
00:30:45,872 --> 00:30:49,165
Aga, I got electrocuted by the mic.

590
00:30:49,519 --> 00:30:52,725
- Yeah, I saw.
- And our lives swapped.

591
00:30:53,550 --> 00:30:55,783
So now, what I’ll do…

592
00:30:55,814 --> 00:30:57,825
- Ah, wait a second…
- I’ll electrocute you…

593
00:30:57,850 --> 00:30:58,895
…to end this…

594
00:30:58,943 --> 00:31:00,903
- Wait, wait!
- …once and for all!

595
00:31:00,928 --> 00:31:05,799
- Wait, just wait. Don’t! Don’t! Don’t!
- I don’t want your life anymore!

596
00:31:05,971 --> 00:31:07,051
BFF! Don’t!

597
00:31:07,673 --> 00:31:08,673
BFF!

598
00:31:14,554 --> 00:31:15,554
BFF!

599
00:31:15,855 --> 00:31:16,855
BFF?!

600
00:31:18,513 --> 00:31:19,513
- Oh!
- Oh!

601
00:31:19,633 --> 00:31:20,608
What happened?

602
00:31:20,633 --> 00:31:21,633
BFF?!

603
00:31:22,583 --> 00:31:24,689
Aga? What happened?!

604
00:31:25,095 --> 00:31:28,468
You got electrocuted! You fainted!

605
00:31:28,493 --> 00:31:29,365
- I’m okay now!
- I’m fine!

606
00:31:29,390 --> 00:31:32,622
How many minutes... how
many seconds was I out?

607
00:31:32,986 --> 00:31:34,473
Just a few seconds, Tso K.

608
00:31:34,685 --> 00:31:35,839
Maybe about three seconds.

609
00:31:36,065 --> 00:31:37,065
Three seconds?!

610
00:31:37,726 --> 00:31:39,466
It felt like a lifetime!

611
00:31:42,097 --> 00:31:43,097
Just three seconds?!

612
00:31:44,280 --> 00:31:45,840
Oh… are you okay now, sis?

613
00:31:47,624 --> 00:31:48,918
Hat do you mean “sis”?!

614
00:31:49,635 --> 00:31:52,625
Don’t call me that, baby!

615
00:31:52,909 --> 00:31:55,083
Can’t you see how macho this is?!

616
00:31:55,264 --> 00:31:56,264
Look!

617
00:31:59,416 --> 00:32:02,195
That’s a bicep, okay! Just the bicep!

618
00:32:02,220 --> 00:32:04,255
Sorry, it’s just that
you look like someone I

619
00:32:04,279 --> 00:32:06,315
know, you know, from
a past life or something.

620
00:32:07,174 --> 00:32:08,514
Oh, really?

621
00:32:08,539 --> 00:32:10,493
Miss Marga, he’s not “sis”!

622
00:32:10,518 --> 00:32:12,910
You can see how
macho Tso K is, right?

623
00:32:12,935 --> 00:32:17,767
Anyway, anyway, it looks like everything’s
fine. The grand reopening continues!

624
00:32:21,344 --> 00:32:24,318
Wait, wait, wait! Iskineport!

625
00:32:24,448 --> 00:32:25,142
Oh?! Oh?!

626
00:32:25,167 --> 00:32:26,167
Water! Water!

627
00:32:27,305 --> 00:32:30,871
Wait, wait! Water, water?!

628
00:32:30,896 --> 00:32:35,783
I’m okay now! I’m okay. I’m good.

629
00:32:41,281 --> 00:32:43,547
Here, have a drink first, Tso K!

630
00:32:45,120 --> 00:32:46,120
What’s this?!

631
00:32:48,501 --> 00:32:51,401
I don’t know! I just panicked!

632
00:32:51,426 --> 00:32:53,135
Good thing it wasn’t juice.

633
00:32:53,933 --> 00:32:55,093
I’d be fine with that.

634
00:32:55,118 --> 00:32:58,327
You’re okay now, Tso K, but…
just rest here for a bit, okay?

635
00:32:58,431 --> 00:33:01,018
Rest? Why rest? No, no!

636
00:33:01,043 --> 00:33:02,603
You’re going to give a speech, right?

637
00:33:02,628 --> 00:33:04,228
- Oh, yeah. I need to say something.
- Are you sure?

638
00:33:04,252 --> 00:33:05,287
Yeah, yeah!

639
00:33:05,502 --> 00:33:06,822
You just got electrocuted!

640
00:33:06,891 --> 00:33:09,257
- I have to speak!
- Ah, okay…

641
00:33:09,282 --> 00:33:09,862
Alright… give it to me.

642
00:33:10,201 --> 00:33:13,727
I have something to say, I
need to expose someone here.

643
00:33:13,752 --> 00:33:14,131
What?!

644
00:33:14,156 --> 00:33:16,073
- You all need to know…
- Chef K!

645
00:33:16,098 --> 00:33:18,979
…the truth! No one’s stopping me!

646
00:33:19,227 --> 00:33:23,093
I’m telling you, there’s
no messing around here!

647
00:33:23,118 --> 00:33:25,648
- BFF…BFF…
- Che-che-chef K…

648
00:33:26,321 --> 00:33:29,014
Alright! Listen up to what I have to say!

649
00:33:31,241 --> 00:33:37,794
This success, Aga doesn’t deserve it!

650
00:33:37,819 --> 00:33:39,252
- What?!
- Oooohh!

651
00:33:39,277 --> 00:33:41,263
- What, why?!
- That hurts!

652
00:33:42,251 --> 00:33:48,463
Because you deserve
even more blessings, Aga.

653
00:33:54,037 --> 00:33:58,660
BFF, I know what you’re going through.

654
00:33:58,911 --> 00:34:03,197
If I were in your position, I
don’t think I could handle it.

655
00:34:05,444 --> 00:34:11,743
But you, everything you have
now, I know you worked hard for it.

656
00:34:14,299 --> 00:34:17,392
You’re such a good person, BFF!

657
00:34:18,566 --> 00:34:19,786
Congratulations!

658
00:34:22,415 --> 00:34:24,062
Long live Kuya Aga!

659
00:34:29,630 --> 00:34:34,601
BFF, thank you so, so much. Thank you!

660
00:34:34,911 --> 00:34:38,885
You’re welcome, you’re welcome!
Let’s give Aga another round of applause!

661
00:34:41,081 --> 00:34:43,594
Congrats, BFF!

662
00:34:43,619 --> 00:34:44,507
Thank you! Thank you, thank
you, thank you, thank you!

663
00:34:44,538 --> 00:34:48,234
Wait, wait, just a second. I
also want to thank all of you…

664
00:34:48,259 --> 00:34:50,896
…because you’ve made our family so happy.

665
00:34:50,921 --> 00:34:52,171
We’re very, very happy.

666
00:34:52,196 --> 00:34:53,229
Yes!

667
00:34:57,276 --> 00:35:00,143
Let’s say goodbye now,
for all the moms out there!

668
00:35:00,219 --> 00:35:06,729
Because through problems and
joys, Pers is first, Pers is the star!

669
00:35:13,860 --> 00:35:15,020
What happened to you, Tso K?

670
00:35:15,067 --> 00:35:16,067
Mmm?

671
00:35:16,848 --> 00:35:18,755
Is that an aftereffect
of the electric shock?

672
00:35:19,179 --> 00:35:21,332
Hmmm! What are you talking about?!

673
00:35:22,137 --> 00:35:26,588
No, I just appreciate this Bake “K” Naman.

674
00:35:27,159 --> 00:35:28,806
Not Bake “A.”

675
00:35:29,482 --> 00:35:32,682
I don’t know, I just
appreciate the life I have.

676
00:35:33,543 --> 00:35:36,196
Wow, life-changing!

677
00:35:37,882 --> 00:35:38,882
Wait...

678
00:35:39,643 --> 00:35:42,705
Okay, but just for today!

679
00:35:43,251 --> 00:35:45,118
Let’s create our own event.

680
00:35:45,563 --> 00:35:50,414
Let’s do something good, as a
thank you for the good life I have now.

681
00:35:50,845 --> 00:35:51,545
Okay?

682
00:35:51,773 --> 00:35:54,880
Free bread here at Bake “K” Naman!

683
00:36:00,027 --> 00:36:01,833
Hey!

684
00:36:03,499 --> 00:36:06,299
Wow! I just announced it,
and you’re already so quick!

685
00:36:06,324 --> 00:36:08,163
You’re so fast!

686
00:36:08,188 --> 00:36:09,188
Hey!

687
00:36:11,045 --> 00:36:15,678
Your debut has been delayed for
five years. It needs to happen this year!

688
00:36:15,748 --> 00:36:18,761
Look at the price of
these gowns, P100,000?!

689
00:36:18,786 --> 00:36:20,614
We don’t have that kind of money.

690
00:36:20,758 --> 00:36:22,685
I want you to meet Ate Elle!

691
00:36:22,710 --> 00:36:23,882
I’ll take care of everything.

692
00:36:23,907 --> 00:36:26,670
I just don’t know what’s the best
thing to do for Tash’s birthday.

693
00:36:26,695 --> 00:36:29,707
- It’s my birthday tomorrow.
- Can we just do a kiss instead?

694
00:36:29,780 --> 00:36:31,646
That’s… possible.

695
00:36:32,505 --> 00:36:33,566
Hey.

696
00:36:33,591 --> 00:36:35,696
Tso K, what’s inside? Is that for Tash?

697
00:36:35,721 --> 00:36:37,900
- I’m good at guessing gifts.
- Just a guess, huh?

698
00:36:39,088 --> 00:36:40,495
Boss Beauty!

699
00:36:40,520 --> 00:36:41,519
Oh, hello!

700
00:36:41,544 --> 00:36:43,576
Here’s your ex-deal gown!

701
00:36:43,601 --> 00:36:44,538
Where did you get this?

702
00:36:44,563 --> 00:36:46,531
At Funeraria Maligaya!

703
00:36:49,881 --> 00:36:53,241
I’ll make sure this
debut will push through.

704
00:36:53,453 --> 00:36:55,207
Should we just back out?
